github.com/unidoc/font
======================

A fork of tdewolff/font (https://github.com/tdewolff/font) by Taco de Wolff.
The upstream MIT license in LICENSE.md applies unchanged.

This fork is maintained for UniDoc's own needs, with no support or stability
guarantees, and may be changed, archived or removed at any time. For general
use, we recommend upstream.

Forked from upstream commit 54f98bb59ee6a56afa51b0c470949b16a4530ca4. The
package API is the same as upstream's, so switching is a change of import path.

Differences from upstream
-------------------------
1. WOFF2 head.flags bit 11 (woff2.go, ParseWOFF2): the WOFF2 spec requires the
   bit to be set, but real fonts (e.g. BarlowCondensed-SemiBold) ship with it
   clear, and Chrome, FreeType and fontTools accept them. Upstream rejects
   such fonts; this fork sets the bit and keeps decoding. The DSIG check stays
   a separate check, so fonts with a DSIG table are still rejected.
2. Go version: go.mod requires Go 1.25. The examples/glyphs example, which
   depends on github.com/tdewolff/canvas and a newer Go, is removed.
3. Upstream's AI-agent instruction files (AGENTS.md, copilot-instructions.md)
   are removed.

The module rename also updates the root module's examples to the new import
path; the nested modules under cmd/ and tests/ are unchanged.

Updating from upstream
----------------------
Rebase this fork's commits onto the new upstream tip, keep the differences
above (drop any upstream has made unnecessary), check that `go test ./...`
passes with Go 1.25, update the commit hash above, and tag a new version.
